y","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"eae7cc249103cef9b112ba64","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"green","chapter":"stool","parent":"MUCOUS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"f07a1284e1cf474b28bb8f4e","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"stitching, stinging","chapter":"teeth","parent":"Merc, nat-m., nux-v., phos., phyt.,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"8e6ae96bfbc9cd89c9b9742d","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"burning","chapter":"urethra","parent":"Cham , clem., equis., graph., ign., kali-n.,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"3c7b50dae6aed56a98fae09e","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"COPIOUS (increased)","chapter":"urine","parent":"CONSTITUENTS, where there is diminution of,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"279ea41ac67d2526d13f1139","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"dark","chapter":"urine","parent":"Benz-ac, brom., Bry., bufo, calc, camph.,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"dca6345d46f7a475d15173da","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96},{"symptom":"white","chapter":"urine","parent":"Am., Ars., Arund., aspar., aur-m.,","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"26f5df4be92996731f209299","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.96}],"sections":[{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"head","label":"Head","startLine":776,"endLine":783,"text":"Depressed and irritable. Head dull, confused.\nPressure in forebead, with nausea, followed by stitches\nin right h\\pochondriLmi. Pain from occiput to frontal\nregion, with bruised sensation of the scalp; worse in\nthe morning. Neuralgic stitches from right to left\nthrough forehead, follow'cd by fl\\ing pains in epi-\ngastrium."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"eyes","label":"Eyes","startLine":784,"endLine":786,"text":"Heavy and hot, with lachryiiiation, with en-\nlarged blood vessels. Eyeballs sore."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"nose","label":"Nose","startLine":787,"endLine":788,"text":"Dry ; inspired air feels cold, nasal passages\nsensitive to it. Coryza, sneezing. Pressure at root of"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"nose","label":"nose","startLine":789,"endLine":791,"text":"Alemlirane over turbinate bones distended and\nboggv, dependent upon hepatic disorders."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"mouth","label":"Mouth","startLine":792,"endLine":794,"text":"Scalded feeling, Afetallic taste. Salivation.\nTongue thickly coated, feels as if scalded."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"throat","label":"Throat","startLine":795,"endLine":803,"text":"Hot, dry, raw, stitching pain into ears when\nswallowing. Follicular pharjmgitis connected with\nhepatic congestion. Veins in pharynx distended and\ntortuous. Throat sensitive to inspired air; feels ex-\ncoriated and constricted, burns like fire on swallowing,\nin afternoon. Early stages of atrophic pharyngitis in\ndried-up, bilious subjects. Hawking of ropy mucus of\nsw^ectish taste."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"stomach","label":"Stomach","startLine":804,"endLine":807,"text":"VV'cight of a stone, wdth gnawing, aching\npain; most manifest about three hours after meals.\nTenderness and fullness in region of liver."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"abdomen","label":"Abdomen","startLine":808,"endLine":815,"text":"Dull aching in liver and epigastrium.\nPain at umbilicus. Throbbing in hypogastrium and\npelvis.\n\ninSCULUS HIPPOCASTAXUM\n\n19"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"rectum","label":"Rectum","startLine":816,"endLine":824,"text":"Dry, aching. Feels full of small sticks.\nAnus raw, sore. Much pain after stool, with prolapse.\nHeemorrhoids, with sharp shooting pains up the back;\nblind and bleeding; worse during climacteric. Large,\nhard, dry stools. Mucous membrane seems swollen and\nobstructs the passage. Irritation caused by ascarides\nand aids their expulsion. Burning in anus with chills\nup and down back."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"urinary","label":"Urinary","startLine":825,"endLine":827,"text":"Frequent, scant, hot urine. Pain in kid-\nneys, especially left and ureter."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"male","label":"Male","startLine":828,"endLine":829,"text":"Discharge of prostatic fluid at stool."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"female","label":"Female","startLine":830,"endLine":834,"text":"Constant throbbing behind symphysis pubis.\nLeucorrhea, with lameness of back across the sacro-\niliac articulation; dark yellow, sticky corroding; worse\nafter menses."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"chest","label":"Chest","startLine":835,"endLine":839,"text":"Feels constricted. Heart’s action full and\nheavy, can feel pulsations all over. Laryngitis; coughs\ndepending on hepatic disorders; hot feeling in chest;\npain around heart."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"extremities","label":"Extremities","startLine":840,"endLine":843,"text":"Aching and soreness in limbs, in left\nacromion process with shooting down arms: finger tips\nnumb."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"back","label":"Back","startLine":844,"endLine":850,"text":"Lameness in neck ; aching between shoulder\nblades; region of spine feels weak; back and legs give\nout. Backache affecting sacrum and hips; worse walk-\ning or stooping. When walking feet turn under. Soles\nfeel sore, tired, and cwell. Hands and feet swell, and\nbecome red after washing, feel full."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"fever","label":"Fever","startLine":851,"endLine":851,"text":"Chill at 4 p. m. Chilliness up and down"},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"back","label":"back","startLine":852,"endLine":854,"text":"Fever 7 to 12 p. m. Evening fever, skin hot and\ndry. Sweat profuse and hot with the fever."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"modalities","label":"Modalities","startLine":855,"endLine":871,"text":"Worse, in morning on awaking, and\nfrom any motion; fioiii moving bowels; after eating.\n\n20 ^THIOPS MERCURIALIS — iETHUSA CYNAPIUM\n\nafternoon, standing. Better, while at rest; walking;\ncool open air.\n\nComparison. — Aiscuhis glabra — Ohio Buckeye —\n(Very paiiiful, dark purple, external haemorrhoids, with\nconstipation and vertigo and portal congestion. Speech\nthick, tickling in throat, impaired vision, paresis.) Aloes;\nC ollinsonia ; Nux; Sulph. Phytolacca (throat dry, more\noften in acute cases.) Negundium Amcricamim — Box-\nelder — (Engorgements of rectum and piles with great\npain, ten-drop doses of tincture every two hours.)"},{"source":"12_boger_synoptic_key","section":"abdomen","label":"abdomen","startLine":24467,"endLine":24475,"text":"Stool, hard, dry; of several colors. RECTUM: sore, as of a burr or sticking pains\nlong after stool; as of a bug crawling from anus (Sul.). Piles, purple, painful, external; with\nBACKACHE (Nux-v.), chest pains, etc. Laming, dull, lumbar pain; small of back gives out;\nrepeated efforts at rising; < walking. Lumbar region or back: as if to break. Bruised pain in\nsacrum and hips. Paralytic heaviness: of arms, spine, feet.\n\nComplementary: Carbo-v. Lach. Mur-ac.\nRelated: Alo. Collin. Pul."}],"corpusPassages":[]}